WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:04.024
Before the coding exercises check whether you can
explain the core ideas

00:00:04.050 --> 00:00:08.796
in your own words First why can a LEFT JOIN followed
by

00:00:08.823 --> 00:00:13.312
a WHERE condition on the right table remove
unmatched left rows Your

00:00:13.339 --> 00:00:19.298
explanation should mention NULL-extended values and
final filtering Second

00:00:19.535 --> 00:00:23.932
can you choose the join type from the population
rule Only matched

00:00:23.959 --> 00:00:28.840
records points toward INNER Every patient points
toward LEFT when patients are

00:00:28.867 --> 00:00:35.268
on the left Full reconciliation points toward FULL
OUTER Third

00:00:35.439 --> 00:00:41.166
can you explain row multiplication without calling
the extra rows duplicates Multiple

00:00:41.192 --> 00:00:48.252
admissions labs and prescriptions create
combinations when joined at patient ID Finally

00:00:48.423 --> 00:00:53.847
can you design a one-row-per-patient result without
inflated counts The safe pattern

00:00:53.860 --> 00:00:57.308
is to summarize each child table to patient grain
before joining it

00:00:57.334 --> 00:00:58.452
to the patient master
